0014: collect_block's search never takes obsidian from a lit nether portal's frame (an obsidian block with a portal
block on one of its faces); an exact cell still can (a frame its builder takes back). With every loaded obsidian in
lit frames, the request has nothing to mine and casts obsidian from lava with its water bucket instead. A production
game (2026-10-13, g71c9f5) mined 12 obsidian out of the shared return portal of earlier games, and the next trip back
from the Nether came out 238 blocks away. With a test (collect-block).

